## Quickstart

{% if orchestrator == 'airflow' -%}
Docker is required for the Airflow stack. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` if you want to
change the default ports, credentials or Airflow user; the defaults work for local
development. Keep `.env` out of git and never put real secrets in it. `make install`
and `make test` use a Python {{ python_version }} virtualenv at `.venv`.

```bash
make install
make up
make test
```

`make up` builds the Airflow image, starts the metadata database, apiserver, scheduler
and DAG processor, waits for health, then unpauses and triggers `weather_pipeline`.
The UI is at <http://localhost:8080> (default login `airflow` / `airflow`; set
`AIRFLOW_PORT`, `_AIRFLOW_WWW_USER_USERNAME` and `_AIRFLOW_WWW_USER_PASSWORD` in
`.env` to change these). `make test` runs the offline Python tests locally.
{% elif warehouse == 'postgres' -%}
Docker is required for the local Postgres warehouse. Copy `.env.example` to `.env`
if you want to change the default connection or host port; the defaults work out of
the box. Keep `.env` out of git and never put real secrets in it. `make install` and
`make test` use a Python {{ python_version }} virtualenv at `.venv`.

```bash
make install
make up
make test
```

`make up` starts the `warehouse-db` service, waits for it to become healthy, then
extracts, loads and builds the dbt models. The database is exposed on
`localhost:5436` (`WAREHOUSE_PORT`) by default.
{% else -%}
A Python {{ python_version }} virtualenv at `.venv` is all you need; `make install`
installs the project into it. Docker is not required for the DuckDB setup.

```bash
make install
make up
make test
```

`make up` extracts, loads and builds the dbt models. The DuckDB file is written to
`data/warehouse.duckdb` and is git-ignored.
{% endif %}

To run without calling the Open-Meteo API, use the recorded fixture:
`PIPELINE_OFFLINE=1 make run`. `make test` and `make ci` always run offline.

## Makefile targets

| Target | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make install` | Installs the project and dev dependencies into `.venv` (editable). |
| `make extract` | Fetches the forecast window and writes raw JSON under `data/raw/`. |
| `make load` | Loads every raw file into the warehouse idempotently. |
| `make run` | Runs `extract` then `load`. |
| `make backfill START=YYYY-MM-DD END=YYYY-MM-DD` | Fetches the historic archive range and writes raw JSON. It does **not** load or rebuild; run `make load build` afterwards. |
| `make build` | Runs the dbt seed, build and source-freshness steps. |
| `make test` | Runs the pytest suite in offline mode. |
| `make lint` | Runs ruff (check and format check) and sqlfluff. |
| `make ci` | Runs lint, tests, an offline `run` and `make build`. |
| `make up` | {% if orchestrator == 'airflow' %}Builds and starts the Airflow stack, then triggers the DAG.{% elif warehouse == 'postgres' %}Starts Postgres, waits for health, then runs `run` and `build`.{% else %}Runs `run` and `build` against the local DuckDB file.{% endif %} |
| `make down` | {% if warehouse == 'postgres' or orchestrator == 'airflow' %}Stops the Compose services. Add `VOLUMES=1` to delete their volumes.{% else %}Prints that there is nothing to stop for DuckDB.{% endif %} |
| `make clean` | Removes `data/`, dbt `target/` and `logs/`, and `.pytest_cache`. |

Set `COMPOSE` to override the detected Compose command, for example
`COMPOSE="docker compose" make up`.

## Configuration

All settings are environment variables. For the Postgres and Airflow options the
Makefile loads `.env` automatically when it exists. `.env` is git-ignored, and
`.env.example` contains placeholders only.

| Variable | Default | Used by |
|---|---|---|
| `PIPELINE_DATA_DIR` | `./data` | Extract and load. Raw files live in `data/raw/`. |
| `PIPELINE_OFFLINE` | unset | Set to `1` to read the recorded fixture instead of calling Open-Meteo. |
{% if warehouse == 'duckdb' -%}
| `DUCKDB_PATH` | `data/warehouse.duckdb` | Python load and the dbt DuckDB profile. |
{% else -%}
| `WAREHOUSE_HOST` | `localhost` | Python load and the dbt Postgres profile. |
| `WAREHOUSE_PORT` | `5436` | Host port for Postgres and the dbt profile. |
| `WAREHOUSE_DB` | `warehouse` | Database name. |
| `WAREHOUSE_USER` | `warehouse` | Database user. |
| `WAREHOUSE_PASSWORD` | `warehouse` | Database password; override outside local development. |
{% endif -%}
{% if orchestrator == 'airflow' -%}
| `AIRFLOW_PORT` | `8080` | Host port for the Airflow UI and API. |
| `AIRFLOW_UID` | `50000` | Host user id used by the Airflow containers. |
| `AIRFLOW_JWT_SECRET` | development value | Airflow API JWT secret; replace outside local development. |
| `_AIRFLOW_WWW_USER_USERNAME` | `airflow` | Initial Airflow admin username. |
| `_AIRFLOW_WWW_USER_PASSWORD` | `airflow` | Initial Airflow admin password. |
| `AIRFLOW_DB`, `AIRFLOW_DB_USER`, `AIRFLOW_DB_PASSWORD` | `airflow` | Airflow metadata database settings. |
| `PIPELINE_HOME` | `/opt/airflow/project` | Container path holding `dbt/` and `data/`. |
{% endif -%}

